# Everything the API image does not need. The build context is uploaded to the Docker
# daemon before the first instruction runs, so anything left in here is paid for on
# every `docker compose build` - and build output copied from the host is worse than
# useless, because it can shadow what the container's own `dotnet publish` produces.

## .NET build output
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage.*.xml

## Source control and CI
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

## Editors and IDEs
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings.user

## Agent and documentation material - none of it compiles
.claude/
docs/
**/*.md
.protected-paths.json
scripts/

## Tests. The image builds src/Todo.Api/Todo.Api.csproj, which pulls in the three
## projects it references and nothing else; the test projects are not part of it.
tests/

## The container's own artefacts, so a nested copy can never end up in the context.
## `**/` because a bare name matches at the root only, and the one Dockerfile here is
## src/Todo.Api/Dockerfile. Excluding it is safe: the builder receives the Dockerfile
## separately from the context.
**/Dockerfile
**/docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

## Local environment
.env
.env.local
